# Vitest rewrites snapshot files with LF endings on every run. Git for Windows
# ships core.autocrlf=true in its system config, so without this line the same
# file is checked out with CRLF — and `git status` then reports it modified
# after every `npm test`, even though the content is byte-identical once the
# endings are normalised (`git diff` shows nothing). Pinning eol=lf makes the
# checked-out copy agree with what the test run writes.
*.snap text eol=lf
